INT. CONVERTED CHURCH - "SYNERGY HUB" - DAY

Pews turned into desks. A stained-glass window glows behind a standing whiteboard. A banner: WE ARE FAMILY.

PENELOPE DRAKE-OYELARIN, 40s, HR lead, headset mic, claps for attention. LIONEL GRAVES, 50s, sales, sits slumped in a pew with a latte. RAMONA TSAI, 30s, engineer, stares at the ceiling.

She rubs her hands together. Beams.

PENELOPE
Okay, team. Icebreaker. Share one word that describes your week.

Lionel sips. Ramona stares.

PENELOPE (CONT'D)
Don't be shy.

LIONEL
Soggy.

PENELOPE
Love that. Ramona?

RAMONA
Fine.

PENELOPE
Fine is a feeling!

Ramona lifts her eyebrows at the ceiling. Doesn't answer.

She writes SOGGY on the whiteboard. Underlines it twice. Caps the marker. It squeaks.

PENELOPE (CONT'D)
Now, trust fall.

LIONEL
No.

PENELOPE
It's a bonding exercise.

LIONEL
I have a back.

She ignores him. Pulls Ramona to the altar step. Ramona goes stiff. Penelope turns her around, steps back, and spreads her arms.

PENELOPE
Whenever you're ready.

Ramona does not fall. She turns, looks at Penelope, then at the whiteboard, then at the window, and takes a long breath.

RAMONA
I quit.

Lionel chokes on his latte. Penelope's smile locks.

PENELOPE
That's not a word that describes your week.

RAMONA
It is today.

She walks down the nave. Her heels echo. Penelope scrambles after her. Lionel lowers his cup.

The main doors bang open. A shaft of daylight cuts the room.

TREVOR ASHBY-NKEMELU, 60s, CEO, in a three-piece suit and a clerical collar for no clear reason, strides in with an iPad.

TREVOR
Who's quitting?

Silence. Ramona stops in the aisle. Penelope stops behind her. Lionel slowly raises his hand.

TREVOR (CONT'D)
Splendid. Lionel, my office. Ramona, my office. Penelope, a word.

He claps once and walks to the pulpit.

PENELOPE
(whispering)
I did the trust fall.

Trevor taps the iPad. His face hardens. Ramona smirks. Lionel gets up and walks, slowly, to the door.
